WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
ChopGate: a NEAR smart contract between an AI agent and its owner's funds.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
It refuses payments that do not match an owner-signed mandate and holds large ones for owner approval.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Step 1: ./check.sh runs the local NEAR sandbox tests, attack suites, demos and UI tests (fast-forward).

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:27.000
It ends with CHECK: ALL OK. This run took 135 seconds.

5
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Scene 1 on testnet: a 0.01 NEAR payment inside the mandate is allowed and paid.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Scene 2: an injected instruction that is not in the mandate is refused. Nothing is paid.

7
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Scene 3: a fake owner key, a forged signature and a wrong caller are all refused.

8
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Scene 4: 0.02 NEAR against a 0.01 NEAR limit is refused: entry_limit_exceeded.

9
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Scene 5: 0.08 NEAR is above the 0.05 NEAR review amount, so the contract holds it.

10
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:16.000
An approval signed by another key fails. The owner's approval pays 0.08 NEAR.

11
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Run B repeats scene 1 with the live JEV judge (p(yes) 0.98). The judge runs off chain.

12
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Limitations: a testnet prototype, not audited, no mainnet deployment.

13
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Each transaction can be checked with the archival RPC command in the README.
